{
  "id": "20827_daihitto",
  "headword": "{大|だい}ヒット",
  "reading": "だいひっと",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "big hit; smash hit; blockbuster",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "big hit; smash hit; blockbuster",
      "explanation": "Something that achieves enormous commercial or popular success, such as a movie, song, product, or book."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20827_daihitto_ex1",
      "japanese": "この{映画|えいが}は{大|だい}ヒットした。",
      "english": "This movie was a smash hit.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20827_daihitto_ex2",
      "japanese": "{新曲|しんきょく}が{大|だい}ヒットを{記録|きろく}した。",
      "english": "The new song recorded a major hit.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20827_daihitto_ex3",
      "japanese": "{予想外|よそうがい}の{大|だい}ヒットとなったこの{商品|しょうひん}は、{発売|はつばい}から{一週間|いっしゅうかん}で{在庫|ざいこ}が{切|き}れた。",
      "english": "This product, which became an unexpected blockbuster, ran out of stock within a week of release.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A combination of the prefix {大|だい} (great/big) and ヒット (hit, from English). Very commonly used in entertainment and business news. Can function as a noun ({大|だい}ヒット) or as a suru verb ({大|だい}ヒットする).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {大|だい}ヒットする: to become a big hit\n- {大|だい}ヒットを{飛|と}ばす: to produce a big hit\n- {大|だい}ヒットを{記録|きろく}する: to register a big hit\n- {空前|くうぜん}の{大|だい}ヒット: unprecedented smash hit\n- {大|だい}ヒット{商品|しょうひん}: blockbuster product\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ヒット: hit — a success, but not necessarily massive\n- {大|おお}{当|あ}たり: jackpot/big success — can also refer to winning a prize\n- ベストセラー: bestseller — specifically for books",
